=== src/Storefront/Framework/SystemCheck/ProductListingReadinessCheck.php:141 (blocking)

The category lookup does not see Dynamic Access restrictions, so the listing check still probes a restricted category and keeps failing for the plugin this PR was written for. Dynamic Access restricts products via `sales_channel.product.process.criteria`, but not categories: from 4.4.0 up to the current 4.5.3 it subscribes to `sales_channel.category.loaded` and sets restricted categories to `active = false` on the loaded entities (`SwagDynamicAccess` `SalesChannelCriteriaSubscriber::addCategoryRuleFilter()`; the `process.criteria` variant is deprecated and no longer registered). That event is dispatched only from `SalesChannelRepository::read()` (`src/Core/System/SalesChannel/Entity/SalesChannelRepository.php:216-231`), which `searchIds()` never reaches (`:187-194`). The probe itself then fails in `NavigationPageLoader::load()` on `if (!$category->getActive())` (`src/Storefront/Page/Navigation/NavigationPageLoader.php:48-49`), not in `CategoryRoute::loadCategory()` as the description says. The new integration tests restrict via `sales_channel.category.process.criteria`, which is why they pass anyway.

I suggest loading the candidates and applying the same `active` check the storefront applies, which covers both criteria-based and loaded-event-based restrictions:

~~~php
$categories = $this->categoryRepository->search($criteria, $context)->getEntities();

// keep the order of the candidates, so child listing pages are preferred over the navigation category
foreach ($candidateIds as $candidateId) {
    if ($categories->get($candidateId)?->getActive()) {
        return $candidateId;
    }
}
~~~

Could we also add an integration test that restricts through a `sales_channel.category.loaded` listener calling `setActive(false)`, the mechanism the plugin actually uses?

